#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d948bac9-62a7-5665-95df-522f8b717271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292417} {:answer/id #uuid "9a755514-92bb-506a-8775-2d1708304b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292418} {:answer/id #uuid "c027f59a-7575-5547-8e1a-bc2ccbcccf58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292419} {:answer/id #uuid "cf27878b-c87e-50bf-a22a-f8c50efcdbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292420} {:answer/id #uuid "b5984bc1-4d99-5874-a48a-f57bbe65a914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf27878b-c87e-50bf-a22a-f8c50efcdbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292420} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ce8856-c1f6-5ff7-bc9a-c230fc99d9dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "919dc14f-ff69-5952-b9d3-1351ffc6437d" :question/math-academy-id "q-104059" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$"}]}
